# Route-parity expectations for the deployed nginx path, checked by
# scripts/route_parity.sh. Format:
#   PATH | EXPECTED-STATUS | EXPECTED-CONTENT-TYPE | BODY-PREDICATE
#
# Every fact here was read from the running deployment (port 5000, inside the
# pod) or from the UI's own URL-construction sites, before any Leptos bundle
# was placed at /opt/frigate/web. That is deliberate: this table is the
# PRE-FLIGHT baseline, describing what nginx and Frigate's React bundle
# return today. A route whose body is the shell -- id="root" and an
# /assets/main-*.js reference -- is currently unmatched by any real location
# and falls back to index.html; that is what the SPA fallback looks like on
# this deployment right now, not a build-specific string. /pkg/corvette.js
# and /pkg/corvette.wasm are two such rows: no /pkg/ location exists yet, so
# they resolve to the same shell as every other unmatched path.
#
# The client-side routes (/, /events, /recordings) and /login use different
# entry chunks -- main-*.js versus login-*.js -- which is what distinguishes
# the two pages the fallback can land on without depending on a content hash
# that changes on every donor rebuild.

/ | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-
/events | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-
/recordings | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-

# location /recordings/ (nginx.conf:164) serves a filesystem JSON autoindex
# of /media/frigate/recordings. This is a DIFFERENT resource from the row
# above with no trailing slash: nginx's try_files fallback only applies to
# the no-slash spelling, so the trailing slash reaches the autoindex instead
# of the SPA shell. A checker that only compared status codes could not
# distinguish this row from the one above -- both return 200.
/recordings/ | 200 | application/json | starts_with:[;contains:"type":"directory"

/login | 200 | text/html | contains:/assets/login-;absent:/assets/main-

/pkg/corvette.js | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-
/pkg/corvette.wasm | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-

/live/webrtc/webrtc.html | 200 | text/html | contains:go2rtc - WebRTC;absent:/assets/main-
/live/mse/api/ws | 400 | text/plain | contains:Bad Request
/api/go2rtc/api | 200 | application/json | starts_with:{;contains:"version"

# No /go2rtc/ location exists in deployed nginx at all, so this path falls
# back to the site's own shell -- an iframe loading the app into itself, at
# HTTP 200, with no error surfaced anywhere. This row exists to document that
# fact and catch a regression in either direction: crates/corvette-ui's live
# tile targets /live/webrtc/webrtc.html above instead, precisely because this
# path is not a real go2rtc endpoint.
/go2rtc/stream.html | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-

